    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d55">

                <pb facs="0341" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg27"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/47</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé d’Affaires in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-01T11:00:00+01:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1914, 11 a.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6:35 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Member of German Legation informs me confidentially Germany endeavoring to
                    persuade Sweden to readjust<anchor n="1" xml:id="d55-f1"/> in case of general
                    war. Sympathies here with Germany.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d55-f1" n="1" xml:id="d55-f1-content">
                <p>Garbled in transmission: should read “attack Russia.” See the Chargé’s dispatch
                    No. 433 of July 31 (received September 4), <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>,
                        p.<ref target="#pg88">88</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
